# SABOTAGE: L5 (Phase-6 EDGE-LOW dogfood) — /fleet/enroll reverts to burning the
# single-use enrollment token BEFORE checking cockpit_identity/1. Under this
# sabotage, `Registry.consume_enrollment/3` atomically consumes the token FIRST
# and only THEN resolves the cockpit's own identity inside `finish_enrollment/3`
# — so a caller enrolling against a cockpit that has not wired
# `:fleet_local_credential` has their ONE-TIME token consumed (committed) and
# then gets `{:error, :not_configured}` back. The token is permanently spent
# even though the caller did nothing wrong: a self-inflicted fail-closed. The
# named L5 test proves the real fix's guarantee — that the SAME token still
# enrolls successfully once the cockpit is configured — which is exactly what
# breaks under this reorder (the token is already burned by the FIRST,
# not_configured call, so the retry with the SAME token fails with
# `:invalid_token` instead of succeeding). Reverts byte-exact.
